# Local worker output, copied into apps/web/public for development.
#
# Root-anchored, for the same reason the HEIC rules below are: an unanchored `reports/` matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, and it was silently swallowing `fixtures/reports/` — the
# tracked report fixtures three tests read. A test whose inputs are gitignored passes on a clean
# checkout by having nothing to check.
/reports/
apps/web/public/reports/
apps/web/public/evidence/
dist-types/

# PDF output
out/

# Local verification samples — real photographs, never committed (see D-104).
# Root-anchored so a deliberate fixture elsewhere is still committable.
/2026-*.heic
/2026-*.jpg
/*.HEIC

# Supabase CLI link state. Per-machine, and it decides which project `supabase db push` writes to
# — a value that must never be set for someone by a checkout. It was tracked until a verification
# task found the repo linked to production while the work targeted a test project.
supabase/.temp/

# Generated by the live verification scripts. The generators are committed, the artifacts are not.
scripts/live/out/
